{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useKeyHold(key): boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useKeyHold.ts#L45","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useKeyHold.ts:45"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React hook that returns whether a specific key is currently being held."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-store"},{"type":"text","value":" to subscribe\nto the global KeyStateTracker and uses a selector to determine if\nthe specified key is held."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"key"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"IndividualKey"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The key to check (e.g., 'Shift', 'Control', 'A')"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"True if the key is currently held down"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function ShiftIndicator() {\n  const isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n\n  return (\n    <div style={{ opacity: isShiftHeld ? 1 : 0.5 }}>\n      {isShiftHeld ? 'Shift is pressed!' : 'Press Shift'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"function ModifierIndicators() {\n  const ctrl = useKeyHold('Control')\n  const shift = useKeyHold('Shift')\n  const alt = useKeyHold('Alt')\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <span style={{ opacity: ctrl ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Ctrl</span>\n      <span style={{ opacity: shift ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Shift</span>\n      <span style={{ opacity: alt ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Alt</span>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"key","text":"key","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useKeyHold(key): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useKeyHold.ts:45](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useKeyHold.ts#L45)\n\nReact hook that returns whether a specific key is currently being held.\n\nThis hook uses `useSelector` from `@tanstack/react-store` to subscribe\nto the global KeyStateTracker and uses a selector to determine if\nthe specified key is held.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### key\n\n`IndividualKey`\n\nThe key to check (e.g., 'Shift', 'Control', 'A')\n\n## Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\nTrue if the key is currently held down\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nfunction ShiftIndicator() {\n  const isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n\n  return (\n    <div style={{ opacity: isShiftHeld ? 1 : 0.5 }}>\n      {isShiftHeld ? 'Shift is pressed!' : 'Press Shift'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\nfunction ModifierIndicators() {\n  const ctrl = useKeyHold('Control')\n  const shift = useKeyHold('Shift')\n  const alt = useKeyHold('Alt')\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <span style={{ opacity: ctrl ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Ctrl</span>\n      <span style={{ opacity: shift ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Shift</span>\n      <span style={{ opacity: alt ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Alt</span>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useKeyHold\ntitle: useKeyHold\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useKeyHold(key): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useKeyHold.ts:45](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useKeyHold.ts#L45)\n\nReact hook that returns whether a specific key is currently being held.\n\nThis hook uses `useSelector` from `@tanstack/react-store` to subscribe\nto the global KeyStateTracker and uses a selector to determine if\nthe specified key is held.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### key\n\n`IndividualKey`\n\nThe key to check (e.g., 'Shift', 'Control', 'A')\n\n## Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\nTrue if the key is currently held down\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nfunction ShiftIndicator() {\n  const isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n\n  return (\n    <div style={{ opacity: isShiftHeld ? 1 : 0.5 }}>\n      {isShiftHeld ? 'Shift is pressed!' : 'Press Shift'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\nfunction ModifierIndicators() {\n  const ctrl = useKeyHold('Control')\n  const shift = useKeyHold('Shift')\n  const alt = useKeyHold('Alt')\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <span style={{ opacity: ctrl ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Ctrl</span>\n      <span style={{ opacity: shift ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Shift</span>\n      <span style={{ opacity: alt ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Alt</span>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
